bic_trace_step.reason:
The newly introduced function qla27xx_copy_multiple_pkt() uses the firmware-reported 'frame_size' to calculate total_bytes and copies data into the fixed-size 'item->iocb' array via memcpy without validating that total_bytes does not exceed the size of the destination (64 bytes). For example, the lines:

  total_bytes = (le16_to_cpu(purls->frame_size) & 0x0FFF) - PURX_ELS_HEADER_SIZE;
  item = qla24xx_alloc_purex_item(vha, total_bytes);
  iocb_pkt = &item->iocb;
  ...
  memcpy(iocb_pkt, &purls->payload[0], no_bytes);

and later in the loop:

  memcpy(((uint8_t *)iocb_pkt + buffer_copy_offset), new_pkt->data, no_bytes);

No bounds check is performed against a maximum allowable size (64 bytes), allowing a buffer overflow when frame_size is larger than 64 bytes.
